  "answer": "The lens maker’s formula is given by: (1/f) = (n - 1)(1/R1 - 1/R2). Here, f is the focal length of the lens, n is the refractive index of the lens material, R1 is the radius of curvature of the first surface of the lens, and R2 is the radius of curvature of the second surface of the lens. This formula is derived by considering the refraction of light through two surfaces of a thin lens and applying the sign convention for distances and radii of curvature.",
